# interplay_lifetime_heap_alias_texture: A 4x4 RGBA8Unorm texture placed at offset 0 of a two-page private heap (type 8, commandType 21, made with the heap's options) and a heap buffer over the same bytes (type 14 at offset 0). The texture reads the bytes the heap was paged from; a fill of the buffer shows in the texture, and a colour fill of the texture (321) shows in the buffer, each in the next exec. Every value is one byte repeated, so what is read does not depend on how the GPU lays the texels out (a texture in a heap is not linear on this GPU). Only the heap is listed: a serializer texture listed faults.
